# Studio deviations for this benchmark - recommendation <tab> reason. The fix leaves these
# alone, the check still runs and reports "exception" with the reason.
1.6.5	HMAC-SHA1 stays allowed for Kerberos only: Active Directory signs Kerberos with AES-SHA1 (aes256-cts-hmac-sha1-96) and a domain join needs it. SSH and TLS have it off (crypto policy module PVS-NO-SHA1-MAC, scope !kerberos).
6.3.3	Leap 16 has one aide package (0.18.8), built without extended-attribute support (aide --version: "xattrs: no"): it cannot apply xattrs. aide.conf asks for it on every audit tool; the other nine attributes are applied and checked.	fix
5.1.24	A gold has no address of its own: sshd cannot be bound to one in the template. The studio binds sshd to the static address of each clone in its first boot (ListenAddress in /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/01-pvs-cis-listen.conf); a clone on DHCP keeps listening on every address.
